# tsc-queue settings.
#
# This file is a TEMPLATE. The installer copies it to ~/.config/tsc-queue.conf
# on the first install and never touches it again, so edit the copy, not this
# file. Your live settings never enter the repository.
#
# Change a value and the next tsc run picks it up. No reinstall is needed,
# except after a change to ROOTS or SCAN: run `tsc-queue install` then.
#
# These settings must live in this file. A task runner such as turbo runs in a
# strict environment mode and drops every TSC_QUEUE_* variable, so exporting
# them in your shell looks like it works and silently does nothing.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- scope ----
# Which directories tsc-queue is allowed to patch. Nothing outside them is ever
# read or written, so no other project's compiler is touched.
#
# Two knobs. Use either, or both. Both take a space separated list.

# ROOTS names each checkout exactly. Use it for a repository you keep in one
# place.
TSC_QUEUE_ROOTS="$HOME/code/my-monorepo $HOME/code/other-repo"

# SCAN names a PARENT directory. Every immediate child holding a package.json
# or a .git is managed. Use it for a directory full of git worktrees: a
# worktree created a second ago is covered with no extra step.
TSC_QUEUE_SCAN="$HOME/worktrees"

# After a change here:
#   tsc-queue install    wrap the new set and update the launchd watcher
#   tsc-queue doctor     list what is covered now
#
# TRAP: narrow the scope in this order, or you strand the shims. The tool only
# walks the directories it currently manages, so a directory you delete from
# these lines can no longer be found and stays wrapped forever.
#   1. tsc-queue uninstall   restores every compiler in the CURRENT scope
#   2. edit these lines
#   3. tsc-queue install

# ----------------------------------------------------------- admission ----
# A CEILING, not a target. Memory decides how many really run below it.
TSC_QUEUE_MAX_SLOTS=6

# The real limiter. A compile starts only when
#   memory in use
# + what the running compiles still have to grow into (peak so far minus what they hold now)
# + this compile's own predicted peak
# stays under this percent of RAM. One 20 GB job therefore runs alone.
TSC_QUEUE_MEM_MAX=85

TSC_QUEUE_ASSUME_MB=1500  # memory guess for a project with no history yet
TSC_QUEUE_STATUS_EVERY=15 # seconds between "still waiting" lines
TSC_QUEUE_HIST_KEEP=10    # how many past runs feed the memory prediction

# ------------------------------------------------------------ advanced ----
# Seconds between launchd safety sweeps that re-wrap a restored compiler.
# TSC_QUEUE_REPAIR_EVERY=30

# WHERE INSIDE a checkout a compiler is found, one glob per line. This is not
# the scope knob; ROOTS and SCAN above decide which directories are patched.
# The default covers npm, pnpm, yarn and bun, and both the JavaScript entry
# point and the native Go compiler. Set this only for an unusual layout, such
# as a monorepo that keeps a copy of typescript inside every package.
# TSC_QUEUE_GLOBS='
# node_modules/typescript/bin/tsc
# packages/*/node_modules/typescript/bin/tsc
# '

# Reverse-DNS prefix for the two launchd job labels.
# TSC_QUEUE_LABEL_PREFIX=io.github.tsc-queue
